                <pb facs="0373" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg308"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.846/61: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-03T09:00:00+03:00">August 3, 1936—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 3—6:36 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>506. My 498, July 28, 4 p.m. Was officially informed last night that cipher
                    communications between legations and their respective governments are now again
                    permitted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
